  "result": "Perfect! All 232 tests pass. The voucher feature is complete:\n\n**Updated src/errors.js:**\n- Added VOUCHER_EXISTS: \"Invoice already has a voucher applied.\"\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- Modified `invoiceTotals` to include `voucher` field (0 if none applied)\n- Formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher` (clamped at 0)\n- Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:\n  - Validates invoice is in draft status (NOT_DRAFT)\n  - Validates no voucher already exists (VOUCHER_EXISTS)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Returns new invoice with `voucher: { code, amount }`\n  - Preserves terms and dueDate\n  - No mutation of original invoice\n- Updated `issueInvoice` to preserve voucher when issuing\n\n**Created test/vouchers.test.js with 20 tests covering:**\n- Adding voucher to draft invoice\n- Rejecting on non-draft/already-issued invoices\n- Rejecting when voucher already applied (one per invoice)\n- Amount validation (non-integer, zero, negative)\n- invoiceTotals calculations with vouchers\n- Formula verification: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n- Voucher reduces total correctly\n- Immutability of original invoice\n- Preserving terms and dueDate\n- Edge cases: huge voucher amounts, total clamped at 0\n- Multiple line items with various VAT rates\n- Voucher codes with numbers and special characters\n- Sequential voucher attempts",
